{"title":"Tamara Podvysotska","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Tamara Podvysotska","about":{"template":"trestles","image":"assets/IMG_2732.jpg","links":[{"icon":"envelope","text":"Email","href":"mailto:top18@pitt.edu"},{"icon":"google","text":"Google Scholar","href":"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=tZqTatkAAAAJ"},{"icon":"person-badge","text":"ORCID","href":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1048-0349"},{"icon":"file-earmark-person","text":"CV","href":"cv.qmd"}]}},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\nHello and welcome :)\n\nI am a developmental scientist with a background in economics. I study how family economic circumstances shape children's development and young adults' life chances.\n\nMy research sits at the intersection of developmental science,\neconomics, and policy. I completed my Ph.D. in Developmental\nPsychology at the University of Pittsburgh, where my dissertation\nfollowed more than 7,000 young adults over 24 years to examine how\nthe composition and timing of childhood family wealth relate to\noutcomes across education, economic wellbeing, mental health, and\nfamily formation.\n\nI bring an unusual path to this work: before turning to developmental\nscience, I earned a doctorate in economics and spent a decade as a\nprofessor and policy researcher in Ukraine, advising national health\nand social reform efforts in partnership with the World Bank, WHO,\nand the World Economic Forum.\n\nAs an educator with fifteen years of university teaching across two\ncountries, I teach developmental psychology, research methods, and\nquantitative analysis — helping students connect developmental\nscience to the real economic and social conditions of children's\nlives.\n\n[Learn more about me →](about.qmd)\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n\nHello and welcome :)\n\nI am a developmental scientist with a background in economics. I study how family economic circumstances shape children's development and young adults' life chances.\n\nMy research sits at the intersection of developmental science,\neconomics, and policy. I completed my Ph.D. in Developmental\nPsychology at the University of Pittsburgh, where my dissertation\nfollowed more than 7,000 young adults over 24 years to examine how\nthe composition and timing of childhood family wealth relate to\noutcomes across education, economic wellbeing, mental health, and\nfamily formation.\n\nI bring an unusual path to this work: before turning to developmental\nscience, I earned a doctorate in economics and spent a decade as a\nprofessor and policy researcher in Ukraine, advising national health\nand social reform efforts in partnership with the World Bank, WHO,\nand the World Economic Forum.\n\nAs an educator with fifteen years of university teaching across two\ncountries, I teach developmental psychology, research methods, and\nquantitative analysis — helping students connect developmental\nscience to the real economic and social conditions of children's\nlives.\n\n[Learn more about me →](about.qmd)\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"late